# Next.js frontend conventions

## Stack

- Next.js App Router, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, TanStack Query

## Structure

- `src/app/` — routes, layouts, error/loading/not-found
- `src/components/ui/` — shared shadcn primitives
- `src/components/layout/` — shell and layout components
- `src/features/` — feature-specific UI and hooks (add when implementing domains)
- `src/lib/api/` — centralized API client and endpoint helpers
- `src/stores/` — Zustand only for genuine client-side global state (avoid server state here)

## Rules

- Keep server state in TanStack Query
- Reuse `src/lib/api/client.ts` for HTTP calls
- Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` for browser-accessible API base URL
- Avoid giant components; extract focused components
- Do not add npm dependencies without justification
- Match existing ESLint and Prettier setup
